 [17592186554794 1072 #uuid "83abebcd-929f-55a9-a148-d27778f5afb1" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554794 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-6y=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =6 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=6 x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =6 x+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{6 x}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{6 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{6 x}.\n$$" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554783 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554801 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554803 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554804 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554807 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1077 "selection" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554783 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554795 1079 #uuid "86288c86-69a9-5332-8284-b2e77b50cc38" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554796 1080 "y=K e^{3 x^{2} + 8 x}" 131941395359