080 "y=K e^{x^{3} + 4 x^{2}}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554799 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554799 1083 #uuid "929b160c-5f08-5021-837d-b9e46e9dd224" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554800 1080 "y=K + 6 x" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554800 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554800 1083 #uuid "945c6768-8894-517a-abc7-51f95ec1b2e0" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554801 1080 "y=K + e^{2 x}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554801 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554801 1083 #uuid "95d62561-ff51-58c3-b0d5-acccd5a59f19" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554802 1080 "y=K e^{12 x}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554802 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554802 1083 #uuid "982ff9b1-ae32-5e5a-a7dc-2b576b8754e4" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554803 1080 "y=K e^{- 2 x}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554803 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554803 1083 #uuid "a8de1130-c0a9-59bd-a338-4887563a0037" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554804 1080 "y=K + 2 x" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554804 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554804 1083 #uuid "abb416b9-0fa8-57dd-a01e-e19606f19afd" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554805 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554816 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554805 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554805 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}-8xy=3{x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554805 1072 #uuid "abbee2f4-ef8f-5ddd-8e7c-80fb454556f0" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554805 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8xy & =3{x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}y+8xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}+8x)y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}+8x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554806 1080 "y=K - x" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554806 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554806 1083 #uuid "ac436b3f-83c2-5c6e-ab75-9264f928e89f" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554807 1080 "y=K e^{2}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554807 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554807 1083 #uuid "b7f6b842-e80e-541c-9ec3-28a2725bc8b9" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554808 1080 "y=K e^{6 x + 8}" 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554808 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535997 17592186045443 true] [17592186554808 1083 #uuid "bf70